Z||000010||Steven||03-26-2001||06:40 PM||||Just to let everyone know. GM Discontinued that part in May of '99. Dealers price was $14.10, with list price being $23.50. The GM number for this part was 17069228. Call your local dealer, maybe they have one sittin under an inch of dust on a shelf in back. Also for everyone FYI... It was also used on '89 Firebird w/3.8 eng., '88-'89 Bonniviles, '85-'88 Buick Somerset and Skylark '86-'87 Buick Riviera and Reatta. It was used on a couple other, but that should help if you are looking around in a parts yard.<P>------------------<BR> 85 Fiero GT<BR> 3.2 Liter Under Construction||||reg||1
Z||000011||fyerstarter||03-26-2001||07:01 PM||||Thanks fierosound. I'll def look into it. As for the plug wires it looks like they are for the v8's on the page you linked to. Did you just use those and toss the two extras?  Do you by any chance have the part number or order number of the set you have that I can use to order from this company?<P>Thanks,  you rule  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000012||fierosound||03-26-2001||08:56 PM||||87ECO5...<P>The paint on the aluminium heat shields and mid/lower intakes is Rust-oleum V2116 High Temperature Aluminium  <A HREF="http://12.15.48.56/ibg/products/hard_hat/default.asp" TARGET=_blank>http://12.15.48.56/ibg/products/hard_hat/default.asp</A> <P>Fyrstarter...<P>As in the message above, #074224 IS the part number for the 6-cyl set in RED<BR>||||reg||1
